# Deployment-host credential material. .env is already ignored above; these
# are the files the wingrc_app cutover leaves beside it on a deployment host
# (the generated role password, and the pre-cutover .env backup). Neither
# should ever be committable by an accidental `git add -A` on that host.
.wingrc_app_pw
.env.*.bak
.env.bak

# Bench/CI credential material, as defence rather than because a token is in
# use. Reading CI status needs no credential at all: this repo is public, so
# run conclusions and per-job/per-step results come back from
# api.github.com unauthenticated (raw log download is the one thing that
# 403s, and a bench reproduction beats a log anyway). A token is only needed
# to *write* -- opening a PR, or merging one. If one is ever introduced, keep
# it outside every checkout, read it as GH_TOKEN="$(cat <path>)", and never
# pass it as an argument, where it lands in shell history and the process
# table. These patterns exist so a stray copy cannot be committed by an
# accidental `git add -A`.
gh_pat_*
.gh_token
